      "writtenOn": "2025-02-03T19:19:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In CrosEC, RW_FWID FMAP section is pointing to the data of the EC_RW section. For some time, binman was not able to create such FMAP, because overlapping was not supported. But after support was added, Wai-Hong Tam preapred [CL](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/4961894) that introduces one `rw-fwid` node (+ necessary linker magic) that works in EC style. All you need to do is including `cros/integrated_fwid.dtsi` in `helipilot.dts`, see my [CL](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5273515). It should just work.\n\nYou can check if the address is correct using `dump_fmap -h build/zephyr/helipilot/output/ec.bin`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "635402fe0febe63e3b7cc59da0a314f11a938758",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
